droxymethyl)methyl-3-aminopropanesulfonic acid (TAPS) is a zwitterionic ionic buffer that is widely used in capillary electrophoresis. As one of the key biological buffers, it maintains the required pH of the medium and exhibits various properties such as high water soluble, highly inert, and stable nature and extremely low absorbance of ultraviolet-visible (UV-vis) light. TAPS buffer also aids in stabilizing lysozyme against thermal denaturation. It is widely used in biology and biochemistry.\nL186: ### Application\nL187: \nL188: TAPS sodium salt has been used along with filtered natural sea water (FSW) to stain live or fixed embryos.\nL189: \nL190: * * *\nL191: \nL192: ## Compare Similar Items\nL193: \nL194: 【17†View Full Comparison】\nL195: \nL196: * * *\nL197: \nL198: Show Differences\nL199: \nL200: [Input]\nL201: \nL202: 1 of 1\nL203: ###### This Item\nL204:  | T5130  | T9659\nL205: --- | --- | ---\nL206: 【18†Sigma-Aldrich T0647 TAPS sodium salt】[Button: Quick View]  | 【19†Sigma-Aldrich T5130 TAPS】[Button: Quick View]  | 【20†Sigma-Aldrich T9659 TAPS】[Button: Quick View]\nL207: description≥99% (titration)  | description≥99.5% (titration)  | description BioXtra, ≥99.5% (titration)\nL208: assay≥99% (titration)  | assay≥99.5% (titration)  | assay≥99.5% (titration)\nL209: Quality Level 200  | Quality Level 400  | Quality Level 400\nL210: application(s)diagnostic assay manufacturing  | application(s)diagnostic assay manufacturing  | application(s)diagnostic assay manufacturing\nL211: form crystalline powder  | form crystalline powder  | form powder\nL212: solubility water: 0.33 g/mL, clear to slightly hazy, colorless  | solubility water: 0.5 g/mL, clear, colorless  | solubility H_{2}O: 1 M, clear, colorless\nL213: impurities≤1% water content (Karl Fischer)  | impurities-  | impurities≤0.1% Insoluble matter, ≤0.005% Phosphorus (P)\nL214: * * *\nL215: ### Still not finding the right product?\nL216: \nL217: Explore all of our products under 【21†TAPS sodium salt】\nL218: \